    "question": {
      ":question/id": "daf12fe8-bb11-5fd8-a3b3-59d7ece27403",
      ":question/problem": "$\\int 17 {e}^{8 x + 3}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "If we let $u=8 x + 3,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=8\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{8}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 17 {e}^{8 x + 3}\\,\\text{d}x&=\\int 17{e}^{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{8}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ &=\\frac{17}{8}\\int {e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ &=\\frac{17}{8}{e}^{u}+C \\\\ &=\\frac{17 {e}^{8 x + 3}}{8}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
