      ":question/problem": "What is $\\int 17 {e}^{- 6 x - 2}\\,\\text{d}x$?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "If we let $u=- 6 x - 2,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-6\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\\text{d}x=- \\frac{1}{6}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 17 {e}^{- 6 x - 2}\\,\\text{d}x&=\\int 17{e}^{u}\\cdot - \\frac{1}{6}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ &=- \\frac{17}{6}\\int {e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ &=- \\frac{17}{6}{e}^{u}+C \\\\ &=- \\frac{17 {e}^{- 6 x - 2}}{6}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
